`git diff origin/main HEAD -- test/integration/screenshots/` shows **78 modified PNGs**, and per-blob comparison shows:

- **0 of 78** match the main that was merged here (`b5312576b`);
- **56** are byte-identical to the branch's own 2026-10-04T23:22Z WIP-auto-save blobs (`36239623c`) — i.e. the merge conflict resolution kept the branch side for these files, discarding main's golden updates from gh-1225 (`78105dce0`, which re-recorded 89 files to green the nightly) and #860 (`9237d5ff7`);
- the remaining 22 match neither side.

Nothing in this PR's ticket, description, or "How to verify" touches the TUI — the js-apps skill, the error channel, the pre-flight gate, and the `composer_echo` timing change do not alter any rendered screen — so these binary changes are pure merge noise. Main's goldens are the authoritative recordings of main's UI; merging this PR would (a) revert main's gh-1225/#860 golden fixes, and (b) leave the visual suite comparing against recordings made on a different code state — a coin flip for red `cli_visual`/nightly on main.

**Fix**: `git checkout origin/main -- test/integration/screenshots/` and commit. If any screenshot legitimately changes because of this PR (none should — no TUI code changed), re-record it on top of main's set with an explicit note in the PR description.
